<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine Jan-Feb trade deficit at $1.96 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippine Jan-Feb trade deficit at $1.96 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine trade deficit widened to $1.96 billion in the first two months of the year compared with $1.582 billion in the same period last year, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The country posted an $814 million deficit in February versus a year ago's $766 million deficit.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE    Jan-Feb 97  Jan 97   Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p>    Exports		   4,685	1,692     3,014</p>
<p>    Imports		   7,356	2,837     4,596</p>
<p>    Trade balance	  -1,960     -1,145    -1,582</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE    Feb 97	Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p>    Exports		   1,812	1,692     1,594</p>
<p>    Imports		   2,626	2,837     2,360</p>
<p>    Trade balance	   -814	-1,145	-766</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in million US dollars</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom +63 2 8109638 Fax 8176267</p>
